#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose the settings for your account, the patient, the display, and the connections."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Account settings belong to you and follow you to every tenant. Patient record, therapy, sharing, and connectors belong to the selected tenant."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Open a category from this page or the Settings menu. Platform administrators also see Platform administration. Setup starts the guided onboarding checklist again."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Each category controls the matching part of Nocturne: sign-in, patient details, display, therapy context, reminders, data sources, or sharing."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "If a category or control is not visible, your role does not include the necessary permission. Ask an owner of the tenant. Settings always require sign-in, also on a public site."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Manage how you sign in: profile picture, passkeys, linked sign-in methods, authenticator apps, and recovery codes."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Your signed-in account. Account details shows your subject ID, the expiry time of your session, and the roles and permissions you hold in the selected tenant."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Add a passkey and give it a name. Link an external provider, such as Google, Microsoft, or GitHub. Add an authenticator app with the QR code and its 6-digit code. Generate recovery codes and keep them private."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Passkeys and linked providers are primary sign-in methods. An authenticator app is a second step: after you add one, each sign-in also requires its code."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "You cannot remove your only primary sign-in method. Add another one first. An authenticator app alone cannot sign you in. The providers you can link are the ones an administrator configured."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Nocturne makes 8 recovery codes. Each code works once. When you generate new codes, all old codes stop working immediately. Use a code when you lost all passkeys and linked providers."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "No sign-in method left"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "If you have no passkey, provider, or recovery code, the server administrator can set NOCTURNE_RECOVERY_MODE. This temporary mode lets you register a new passkey. It requires access to the server environment."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Limits per account"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "You can register up to 20 passkeys and up to 10 authenticator apps. Give each one a name, so that you can identify the device later."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Describe the person whose data this tenant holds: clinical details, devices, and insulins."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Details that you or another member enter. Discovered sources lists device streams from recent readings that are not linked to a device yet."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Clinical information holds diabetes type, diagnosis date, date of birth, sex, preferred name, pronouns, timezone, and weight. Use Devices and Insulins to add, edit, sort, or delete entries."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "The timezone sets the local hours for alerts, schedules, and analytics. Sex and date of birth select the typical ranges in sleep reports. A rapid-acting insulin sets the insulin action time."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Changes here do not change readings or treatments. Delete removes an entry permanently. Set an end date when you stop using a device or insulin, so that the history stays correct."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Timezone and weight"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "A changed timezone applies from the moment you save. Past data keeps its times. A changed weight is added to Weight history, and the previous entry stays."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose a model from the catalog, or enter a manufacturer and model. A catalog CGM also adds sensor trackers. A catalog pump adds pod, site, or reservoir trackers. Use the arrows to rank overlapping devices of one category."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Nocturne lists sources that sent readings but have no device in the patient record. Select Register as device to link a source to a device entry."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Insulins and action time"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose a category and formulation. The formulation fills in the duration of insulin action, peak, and concentration, and you can change them. Nocturne uses the action time of the rapid-acting insulin for insulin on board and predictions. If another app manages the profile, Nocturne uses the action time of that profile instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose how Nocturne looks for you: theme, units, formats, charts, dashboard, and help."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Most choices are saved to your account and follow you to other devices. Help display choices are saved in this browser. Default chart range, tracker pills, and glucose processing apply to the whole tenant."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose a color theme, glucose range colors, light or dark mode, language, units, and formats. Configure the dashboard widgets, status pills, chart lines, and the browser tab here."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Display choices change how values look. Stored readings and their units stay the same. Theme changes take effect immediately."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "A choice that applies to the whole tenant changes the display for every member. The language preference syncs to your account only when you are signed in."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Units and formats"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Glucose shows in mg/dL or mmol/L. Food energy shows in kJ or kcal. The regional format sets the date order, month names, and the first day of the week. You can show HbA1c as HbA1c or A1c."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Charts"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Default chart range sets the hours that the dashboard chart shows. Lines and points use one color, the threshold bands, or a continuous gradient. Chart patterns add textures, so that color-blind readers can tell the series apart."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose and sort the widgets above the glucose chart and the status pills beside the glucose value. Tracker pills show the age of running trackers. Set the visibility of each tracker in Notifications & trackers."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Glucose processing"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Some sources send smoothed and unsmoothed values. Choose which value Nocturne shows, or Default for the value that the source reports. Source default rules choose per app or device, and the first matching rule wins."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Browser tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "The browser tab can show the glucose value, direction, and change in its title and icon. Flash on alarms makes the title and icon flash during urgent glucose levels."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Help display"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Help visibility shows the full help bar, only the library icon, or no help. Layout opens help as a book, a right drawer, side by side, or in place of the page. Close help with the book, the close button, or Escape. Your page and its inputs stay in place."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Inspect therapy profiles: basal rates, carb ratios, insulin sensitivity, and target ranges."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Profiles usually come from your diabetes app, such as AAPS, Loop, or xDrip+, through an uploader or connector. A profile synced from such a source is read-only here."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Select a profile to see its schedules. Make default chooses the profile that applies when no switch is active. Switch records a profile switch. You can edit the target range of a profile that Nocturne manages."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Insulin on board, predictions, scheduled basal, and target overlays use the profile that applied at each moment."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "A scheduled basal rate does not prove that the pump delivered it. Change a read-only profile on the source device. Discuss therapy changes with your diabetes care team."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "A switch starts now. It can scale the profile from 30 to 250 percent and shift the schedule by -23 to 23 hours. A temporary switch lasts 1 minute to 7 days. Without a duration, it runs until you end it or another switch replaces it."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "What a switch does not do"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Nocturne only records the switch. It is not sent to your pump, and AAPS and Nightscout followers do not see it. If your AID system reports the profile that the pump runs, Nocturne calculations follow that reported profile."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Delete a profile"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "You cannot delete the only profile or the default profile. Deleting removes its schedules and their history. Readings and treatments stay. A synced profile comes back on the next sync. To prevent that, stop profile sync at the source."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Set the sleep times and the compression low detection that overnight analysis uses."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Your saved settings and the readings stored in this tenant."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose a typical bedtime and wake time. Enable automatic detection of compression lows. Members with full access also see Data maintenance."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "The sleep schedule sets the overnight window for analysis. Detection notifies you about possible compression lows, so that you can review them."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "A detection is a suggestion, not proof that a reading is wrong. A change to these settings does not change existing readings."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "A compression low is a falsely low CGM reading, caused by lying on the sensor. When you confirm one, Nocturne keeps a record for you. The readings stay in your reports and statistics."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Data maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Deduplicate records links readings, treatments, and state spans that different sources uploaded for the same event. It matches records within 30 seconds by time and value. The original records stay, so you can run it again. Remove demo data deletes only the generated sample data."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Track sensors, sites, reservoirs, batteries, appointments, and other recurring events, with reminders."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Tracker definitions, presets, and running and completed trackers in this tenant. Your pump, loop, or a connector can also start and complete trackers."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Active shows running trackers. Start, complete, or record a reservoir level there. History lists completed trackers. Definitions holds reusable templates. Presets start a tracker in one step."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Tracker ages and urgency appear as pills on the dashboard. Notification thresholds send reminders through alert rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "A reminder does not confirm that you changed the device. If you delete a definition, its running trackers stay, but you cannot start new ones. Completing a tracker and editing its definition are different actions."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Duration and event trackers"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "A duration tracker runs for its expected lifespan from the start, written as 10x24 or 10d. An event tracker is scheduled for one date and time, such as an appointment. A reservoir definition can also alert when the estimated level falls below a number of units."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Add up to 4 thresholds with a level: Info, Warning, Hazard, or Urgent. For a duration tracker, positive hours count from the start and negative hours count back from expiry. For an event tracker, negative hours are before the event."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Reminder delivery"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Each threshold gets a managed alert rule after you save the tracker. Use Channels on a threshold to open that rule and choose where the reminder goes."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Automatic restart"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose events under Restart automatically on. When your pump, loop, or a connector reports one, the running tracker completes and a new one starts. Use the notes filter to keep two trackers apart, such as a left and a right site."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Dashboard and Nightscout"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Dashboard visibility shows the pill always, never, or after a threshold level. Event integration can create a treatment event at start or completion, for the Nightscout CAGE and SAGE pills."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "See the browsers that are signed in to your account, and sign them out."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "The list of your active sessions on the server, with device description, last activity, and IP address."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Sign out one session, or select Sign out everywhere else to keep only this device. Members who can change tenant settings also see the API reference switch."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "A browser that you sign out must sign in again."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Signing out a session does not delete data. If you sign out the session you use now, you are signed out here."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Connected apps, uploaders, and API tokens are in Connectors & apps. Members, invites, guest links, and public access are in Sharing & privacy. Revoke each one on its own page."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "The switch publishes the interactive API reference and the OpenAPI specification on this address, for anyone, without sign-in. Your data stays behind sign-in. Keep it off unless you build against the API."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose who can see this tenant's data, and what they can do with it."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Members, invites, membership requests, roles, guest links, and the public link of this tenant."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Invite people with a link, edit the roles of a member, review requests, create guest links, and configure public access. The sections you see depend on your own permissions."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Roles and direct permissions decide which pages, data, and actions each member gets."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Anyone with a guest link or the public link sees what it allows. Revoking stops new access, but it does not remove copies that someone already made."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Invite links"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "An invite link lets a person join after they sign in. Choose roles, optional direct permissions, and an expiry from 1 to 90 days. By default, a link works once. Select Allow multiple uses for more people. People who joined keep access after the link expires."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Members and roles"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Edit opens the roles and direct permissions of a member. You cannot change your own roles. System roles are fixed. A custom role combines the permissions that you choose. Removing a member ends their access to all tenant data."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "This option limits a member, invite, or request to the most recent 24 hours of data. Owners and members who manage tenant settings cannot be limited. A limited member cannot give anyone wider access."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "A guest link gives read-only access to the categories you choose, for someone without an account. The code works once. The first device that uses it stays signed in for 48 hours. Select New code for another device."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Public access gives anyone with your link read-only access to the categories you select, without an account. Choose All history or Last 24 hours. Regenerate stops the old link immediately."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "When membership requests are on, people who reach your profile can ask to join. Nothing is granted automatically. You choose the roles when you approve a request."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "See which data changed. If read access logging is on, also see who read patient data."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Audit records that the server keeps for this tenant. Data changes are always recorded. Data access is recorded only when read access logging is on."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Data changes and Data access each have a date filter. The list shows the most recent entries in the range. Narrow the dates to see older entries. Members who manage audit settings can change logging and retention."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Use the log to see who changed a record, a setting, or a permission, and when."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Only events that the server recorded appear. Reads from before read access logging was on are not in the log. Viewing the log requires the audit.read permission."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Retention"
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Each log keeps entries for its retention in days. An empty field uses the platform default. Data change retention must be at least the retention of deleted records. Then a deletion stays attributed while the record can be restored."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Copy historical data from an existing Nightscout into Nocturne."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "The Nightscout site, with its URL and API secret, or its MongoDB database, with connection string and database name."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Choose the source and enter its credentials. Test connection shows the number of entries and treatments it found. Optionally choose a date range. Then select Start migration and follow it under Progress."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
msgid "Imported entries, treatments, device status, profiles, food, and activity appear in the normal charts and reports."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/help/settings.svelte.ts
